The Art of Insight in Science and Engineering — Mahajan (@ql-source-insight: 0, is #book, #part-of @ql-sources) { r_2YTYM3AC7KGP77Q5W1TT7S88KR
Sanjoy Mahajan. The Art of Insight in Science and Engineering: Mastering Complexity. MIT Press, 2014. English. ISBN 978-0-262-52654-8.

[Authorized complete book and contents](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/res-6-011-the-art-of-insight-in-science-and-engineering-mastering-complexity-fall-2014/pages/open-textbook/) · [Earlier course, readings, and worked problem sets](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-055j-the-art-of-approximation-in-science-and-engineering-spring-2008/).

Read Part I first, then Part II alongside units and balances, then Part III in the later modelling study. The 2014 book's chapter sequence is Divide and conquer; Abstraction; Symmetry and conservation; Proportional reasoning; Dimensions; Lumping; Probabilistic reasoning; Easy cases; Spring models. The earlier course notes have a different organization and some missing material, so use the 2014 book for the whole-book assignment.

MIT OCW explicitly offers the complete 2014 book under CC BY-NC-SA. Preserve its precise edition notice, the author, publisher, and component credits before redistribution or adaptation. The reference and download remain external. The official description, contents, and availability checked on 28 October 2026.

**Return:** [Quantitative literacy sources — books, standards, and articles](../Sources.lingua#r_7MMXWNA1B4YGA271KMHPPJEK9Q).
